module gunbc.plans.inert_layer_lens

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetirement, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock }
import gunbc.plans.md_helpers { p }
import gunbc.design_ruling { project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts }

fn inert_layer_lens_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    p(text: "**Goal:** expose declared concepts unreachable from live run-roots. Compute declared ∧ ¬reachable over the whole static and reflective reference graph; local consumer counts miss dead clusters. Run and test roots are separate: test-only reachability is “tested but unrun,” never production liveness. The run-inert verdict drives the proposed wall; test coverage is a separately reported dimension."),
    p(text: "**Method:** enumerate exact floor/compiler/emit/CLI roots and reflective host/marker-discovery edges. Every declaration must be reached, named on a shrinking exception roster with a consumer-PR dissolve-on, or deleted. Begin advisory; promote only after roots/bridges are complete and staged-ahead exceptions dissolve. Model-before-consumer is legitimate; an untracked inert population is not. Never gate on expected consumer counts or heuristic importance. Never-constructed arms/unread fields are finer structural observations; “should have more consumers” belongs to redundancy/nicknaming analysis."),
    p(text: "**Owners:** build module reachability over v2.lens.module_graph selection-tier facts; #5433 inert_lens_modules was deleted by #8141 and must not be resurrected inside floor discovery. Reuse concept_index.enumerate_concepts, BindsTo use classification and LayerImportFact projections. Symbol reachability needs whole-corpus BindsTo enumeration, which the original audit lacked; any admitted host bridge shares concept_index’s #5364 dissolution when .dag compile-graph access arrives. Do not fabricate reference sites from declarations. Changes to load-bearing cli_run.rs require the stated escalation before editing."),
    p(text: "**Advisory ranking:** arm/field counts, return-type richness and Plan/Account/Receipt/Schedule/Demand/Policy names rank apparent load-bearing importance only. Inertness and vacuity share relation machinery but not verdicts: vacuity uses ProvenDuplicate | ProvenIndependent | Unknown oracle provenance and independent-oracle/construction/deletion remedies, not Share. Consolidate mechanisms without merging meanings."),
    p(text: "**Related instances:** doc reachability uses kind-specific roots (DESIGN/ROADMAP for plans, operational index for runbooks), Markdown links and .dag-comment bind references. Add a document’s inbound edge in its PR. Dangling links can use filesystem_read BFS; orphan detection also needs universe enumeration. #5484’s doc_reachability_project host reader supplies doc_graph_orphan_count/dangling_link_count until list-dir/compile-graph access permits its deletion. Witness: dag/test/claim/doc_reachability_witness.dag and synthetic RED/GREEN controls. Do not infer a directory universe from reached files."),
    p(text: "**Distinct landed observation:** v2.lens.inert_carrier / inert_carrier_project diagnoses self-tested carriers with no non-test consumer outside their declaration block. That coverage-by-illusion rule, its shrinking/stale roster and floor/host controls do not establish run-root reachability; the code Tier-1/Tier-2 reachability target remained unbuilt in the audit. Both host readers dissolve at #5364. These are historical standings, not current execution receipts."),
    p(text: "**Validate/open:** independently reproduce dead clusters, test-only nodes, reflective consumers, reached modules with dead symbols, separate runbook roots, orphans and dangling links; restored defects must fail. Confirm all runtime roots, choose module-first versus symbol-first delivery, and move the doc dangling half to pure .dag without waiting for orphan enumeration. The [dated census and landing receipts](https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/blob/06d3c1c3149a7420c4a548b9aba9b15c721c635d/dag/gunbc/plans/inert_layer_lens.dag) retain examples: compute_fabric carriers were later dissolved by #5904, and RealizationObjective.goals was deleted; rederive the class instead of treating those rows as current inventory. The permanent lens survives; its exceptions and this plan retire on the conditions below."),
  ]
}

data inert_layer_lens_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly { ruling: project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts },
  slug: "inert-layer-lens",
  title: "The inert-layer lens — modeled but unreached",
  body: inert_layer_lens_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Delete this doc when the inert-layer lens family it specifies is fully built and self-describing in the carriers: the still-unbuilt code Tier-1/Tier-2 target class (`v2.lens.inert_layer` over the run-roots, covering `CacheLayerPlan` / `WorkDemand` / `execution_receipt_digest`) has landed as fail-closed floor witnesses alongside the already-live doc-graph (gunbc#5484) and inert-carrier (Lane 7) instances — at which point the rule \"reachable from a run-root, on the exception roster, or deleted\" is enforced by execution across all three substrates and this design prose is superseded by the lenses themselves (the lens never dissolves; this doc does, per DESIGN §6's mark-on-carrier-is-authority).")
  }
}
